.\"-------.\" s m i l e y . 1.\".\" DaviD W. Sanderson.\"-------.hy 0.TH SMILEY 1 "April 1, 1991".SH NAMEsmiley \- print or explain smileys.SH SYNOPSIS.B smiley.RB [ \-V ].RB [ \-e ].RB [ \-l ].RB [ \-f ].RI [ smiley... ].br.SH DESCRIPTION.I Smileyis a program for smiley junkieswho like to have all the smileys at their fingertips..PPThe options have the following meaning:.TP .B \-VPrint the version of the programand the number of faces and definitions..TP .B \-eExplain the face found in the environment variable.BR SMILEY ..TP.B \-lPrint a listing of all the known smileys, with explanations..TP.B \-fPrint a random smiley, face only..TP.I smileyExplain the given smiley..PPWhen invoked with no arguments,.I smileyprints a random smiley with an explanation..SH EXAMPLEHere are some.IR ksh (1)functions that put a smiley into your prompt..TP.BR ps1sed (\|)Transform the standard input so that it will display properlywhen it is made part of.B PS1in.IR ksh .(That is, quote \0!\0$\0\e\0 if they appear.)These are the transformations:.sp.\"	!	\(->	\e\|!\|\e\|!	!	\(->	!\|!.br	$	\(->	\e\|$.br	\e	\(->	\e\|\e.br.IPNote that a \0!\0must be doubled instead of quoted with \0\e\0in order to display..RS.nf.ta .5i +\w'sed \''u.sp.ne 5ps1sed\|(\|){.\"	sed 's/!/&&/g.\"#		s/\\/&&/g.\"#		s/[!$]/\\&/g'.\"		s/[!$\\]/\\&/g'.\".\"	sed \'s/\^!/&&/g.\"		s/[!$\|\e\|\e\|]/\|\e\|\e\|&/g\'.\"	sed \'s/\^!/&&/g		s/[$\|\e\|\e\|]/\|\e\|\e\|&/g\'}.sp.DT.fi.RE.TP.BR ps1 (\|)Put a new smiley into.BR PS1 .Use.I ps1sedto make sureany characters in the smileythat are special to the shellare quoted appropriately..RS.nf.sp.ne 5ps1\|(\|){.\"	export SMILEY="`smiley -f`".\"	PS1=`print -r - "$SMILEY" | ps1sed`" "	export SMILEY="`smiley \-f\|`"	PS1=`print \-r \- "$SMILEY" | ps1sed\|`" "}.fi.RE.SH CAVEATSThe list of smileys is the personal collection of the author,so there are bound to be some missing..PPMultiline smileys and the ``invisible smiley'' are absent from.I smileybecause the author does not want a multiline or invisible prompt..SH AUTHORDaviD W. Sanderson	(dws\|@cs.wisc.edu).SH COPYRIGHT\&.br.if n (C).if t \s+8\v'+2p'\fB\(co\fR\v'-2p'\s0\s+2Copyright 1991 by DaviD W. Sanderson\s0